WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.067
-Finally, you guys,
I'm very excited.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.234
It is St. Patrick's Day today.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.000
I mean, this is a big deal.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.534
I love it.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.601
But I got to say, every year,
people focus too much

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.133
on the stereotypes
and not enough on what makes,

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.701
really, St. Patrick's Day
and Ireland so special

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.901
and, to show you what I mean,
I actually wrote a little song.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.033
Roots, can I get a note?

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.567
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.601
[ Irish accent ]
♪ Oh oh ♪

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:24.734
♪ The 17th of March is here ♪

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.801
♪ The day has got me thinkin' ♪

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.801
♪ St. Patty's Day and Ireland ♪

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.701
♪ So much more than drinkin' ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.300
♪ The cliffs of Moher
are gorgeous ♪

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.400
♪ If great heights
you do not fear ♪

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.267
♪ A lovely place
to see the view ♪

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.167
♪ And crack an ice cold...
water ♪

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.100
♪ Go and see the Blarney Stone ♪

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.000
♪ And kiss it,
if you're frisky ♪

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.234
♪ Then wash your mouth out
with a giant shot ♪

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.601
♪ Of Irish...LaCroix ♪

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.367
♪ There are no snakes
on Emerald Isle ♪

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.300
♪ No creepy crawly scalies ♪

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.467
♪ So, just relax,
enjoy some coffee ♪

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.534
♪ Mixed with creamy oat milk ♪

00:00:58.534 --> 00:00:59.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:03.000
♪ Pick a four-leaf clover
hidden underneath a shrub ♪

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.701
♪ Then show it off
to all your mates ♪

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.300
♪ Down at the local library ♪

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.901
♪ To Dublin or to Galway,
if you want to see a sight ♪

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.968
♪ And watch two old men argue
till it turns into a... ♪

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:16.033
Cordial acceptance
of their differences.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:18.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:21.834
[ Cheering ]

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.934
♪ Now, my tune is over ♪

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.000
♪ Time to climb into me bunk ♪

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.567
♪ That's all to say
this St. Patrick's Day ♪

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.467
♪ Screw it, let's get drunk ♪

